q(n,6,['options',2,'explanation'],'The attacker need not break TLS; it establishes its own legitimate encrypted connections and abuses HTTP/2 stream processing.','Cryptographyis involvedbutnotbroken.')
q(n,6,['options',3,'explanation'],'Such controls can help; exact patches and policies differ. Some implementations also budget stream creation and outstanding backend work.','Not allpatchedserversuseidenticalreset-rateGOAWAYpolicy.')
q(n,6,['workedExample'],'A concurrent-stream cap alone does not bound the rate of stream creation and cancellation. Resets can close protocol streams while dispatched work remains expensive. This can exhaust finite server capacity across attacker connections; it does not imply infinite work or that a single connection produced the reported aggregate attack rate. Mitigations should account for creation/reset work and implementation-specific resource use.','Removeunboundedwork andaggregate398Msingleconnectionimplication;100defaultnotuniversal.')
